  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low bronze lobster creeps on an overlapping eight-leg wave. Its carapace stays steady, rounded feet take clear equal advances, the centered segmented tail follows with restrained pitch and the four antennae make small independent sweeps.",
    "attack": "The large asymmetric pincers open, reach forward and snap in a braced right-left sequence. Whole bent forearms and palms rotate around measured sockets; the genuine fingers close without stretching.",
    "death": "The carapace settles forward/down onto its actual underside; outer limbs relax, eight inner pendant appendages fold aside, both pincers and the centered tail/fan find support. The final pose holds still."
